IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1, PART 10 (OWNERSHIP AND CONTROL OF BROADCASTING COMPANIES, ss 32 to 45). Section 38 is repealed (Act 31 of 2022): no rule.
-- These rules state the 2024 consolidation. The Minister's approvals and satisfaction, and the Authority's approvals, are the Minister's and the Authority's: each is a plain fact asked of the person.
-- Meanings borrowed from the Companies Act 1967 (ss 4, 5, 7, 81) and the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018 are asked as facts, with the section cited.
-- Three passages of the deposit print closing words with a paragraph letter (s 37(4), s 43(9)(d), s 44(1)(b)); s 43(9) is a fork (F-BA-06), the other two are reading notes (R-1, R-2) in NOTES.md.

§ `32. Application of this Part to broadcasting company`

-- src:1815 | 32.—(1) This Part applies to every broadcasting company unless
-- src:1816 | exempted by the Minister under section 60(b).
@ref s 32(1) (src:1815-1816)
GIVEN `it is a broadcasting company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has exempted it under section 60(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(1) this Part applies to the company` MEANS
    `it is a broadcasting company` AND (NOT `the Minister has exempted it under section 60(b)`)

-- src:1821 | (2) In this Part —
-- src:1823 | “broadcasting company” means a company incorporated or
-- src:1824 | registered under the Companies Act 1967 which holds a
-- src:1825 | relevant licence, or a broadcasting holding company;
@ref s 32(2) chapeau and "broadcasting company" (src:1821-1825)
GIVEN `it is a company incorporated or registered under the Companies Act 1967 which holds a relevant licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a broadcasting holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) the company is a broadcasting company` MEANS
    `it is a company incorporated or registered under the Companies Act 1967 which holds a relevant licence` OR `it is a broadcasting holding company`

-- src:1827 | “broadcasting holding company” means a holding company of a
-- src:1828 | company incorporated or registered under the Companies
-- src:1829 | Act 1967 which holds a relevant licence;
@ref s 32(2) "broadcasting holding company" (src:1827-1829)
GIVEN `it is a holding company of a company incorporated or registered under the Companies Act 1967 which holds a relevant licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) the company is a broadcasting holding company` MEANS
    `it is a holding company of a company incorporated or registered under the Companies Act 1967 which holds a relevant licence`

-- src:1831 | “holding company” has the meaning given by section 5 of the
-- src:1832 | Companies Act 1967;
@ref s 32(2) "holding company" (src:1831-1832)
-- Borrowed from section 5 of the Companies Act 1967: asked as a fact.
GIVEN `it is a holding company within the meaning of section 5 of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) the company is a holding company` MEANS
    `it is a holding company within the meaning of section 5 of the Companies Act 1967`

-- src:1834 | “relevant licence” means —
-- src:1836 | (a) any free-to-air licence; or
-- src:1838 | (b) any broadcasting licence under which a subscription
-- src:1839 | broadcasting service may be provided,
-- src:1841 | which permits broadcast which is capable of being received
-- src:1842 | in 50,000 dwelling-houses or more, but does not include any
-- src:1843 | class licence; or
-- src:1845 | (c) any other broadcasting licence that the Minister may
-- src:1846 | specify in the public interest or in the interests of
-- src:1847 | public security or order, or national defence;
@ref s 32(2) "relevant licence" (src:1834-1847)
GIVEN `it is a free-to-air licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a broadcasting licence under which a subscription broadcasting service may be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it permits broadcast capable of being received in 50,000 dwelling-houses or more` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is another broadcasting licence the Minister specified in the public interest or in the interests of public security or order, or national defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) the licence is a relevant licence` MEANS
    `it is another broadcasting licence the Minister specified in the public interest or in the interests of public security or order, or national defence`
    OR ((`it is a free-to-air licence` OR `it is a broadcasting licence under which a subscription broadcasting service may be provided`) AND `it permits broadcast capable of being received in 50,000 dwelling-houses or more` AND (NOT `it is a class licence`))

-- src:1851 | “sub‑fund”, “umbrella VCC” and “VCC” have the meanings
-- src:1852 | given by section 2(1) of the VCC Act;
@ref s 32(2) "sub-fund", "umbrella VCC" and "VCC" (src:1851-1852)
-- Borrowed from section 2(1) of the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018: asked as a fact.
GIVEN `it is a sub-fund, umbrella VCC or VCC within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) the entity is a sub-fund, umbrella VCC or VCC` MEANS
    `it is a sub-fund, umbrella VCC or VCC within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018`

-- src:1856 | “VCC Act” means the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018.
@ref s 32(2) "VCC Act" (src:1856)
GIVEN `it is the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) the Act is the VCC Act` MEANS
    `it is the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018`

§ `33. Special features of broadcasting company`

-- src:1862 | 33.—(1) A broadcasting company must not, on or after
-- src:1863 | 2 September 2002, appoint a person as its chief executive officer
-- src:1864 | or director, or as the chairperson of its board of directors, unless it has
-- src:1865 | obtained the approval of the Authority.
@ref s 33(1) (src:1862-1865)
GIVEN `the appointment is on or after 2 September 2002, of a chief executive officer, director or chairperson of the board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has obtained the approval of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(1) the broadcasting company has contravened the subsection` MEANS
    `the appointment is on or after 2 September 2002, of a chief executive officer, director or chairperson of the board` AND (NOT `the company has obtained the approval of the Authority`)

-- src:1867 | (2) Unless the Authority otherwise approves, the chief executive
-- src:1868 | officer of a broadcasting company and at least one-half of its directors
-- src:1869 | must be citizens of Singapore.
@ref s 33(2) (src:1867-1869)
GIVEN `the Authority has otherwise approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the chief executive officer is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors who are citizens of Singapore` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(2) the company meets the citizenship requirement` MEANS
    `the Authority has otherwise approved` OR (`the chief executive officer is a citizen of Singapore` AND `the number of directors who are citizens of Singapore` TIMES 2 AT LEAST `the number of directors`)

-- src:1874 | (3) No chief executive officer, director, or chairperson of the board
-- src:1875 | of directors, of a broadcasting company who was appointed before
-- src:1876 | 2 September 2002 is to be permitted by the broadcasting company to
-- src:1877 | act as such on or after that date unless —
-- src:1879 | (a) his or her appointment as chief executive officer, director,
-- src:1880 | or chairperson of the board of directors, of the broadcasting
-- src:1881 | company was approved by the Authority before
-- src:1882 | 2 September 2002; or
-- src:1884 | (b) his or her appointment as chief executive officer, director,
-- src:1885 | or chairperson of the board of directors, of the broadcasting
-- src:1886 | company is approved by the Authority on a written
-- src:1887 | application by the broadcasting company made within
-- src:1888 | 6 months after 2 September 2002 or any longer period that
-- src:1889 | the Authority may allow.
@ref s 33(3) (src:1874-1889)
GIVEN `the person was appointed before 2 September 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment was approved by the Authority before 2 September 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is approved by the Authority on a written application made within 6 months after 2 September 2002 or any longer period the Authority allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(3) the company may permit the person to act as such on or after 2 September 2002` MEANS
    IF `the person was appointed before 2 September 2002` THEN JUST (`the appointment was approved by the Authority before 2 September 2002` OR `the appointment is approved by the Authority on a written application made within 6 months after 2 September 2002 or any longer period the Authority allows`) ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1891 | (4) Where the Authority does not approve the appointment of a
-- src:1892 | person as chief executive officer, director or chairperson of the board
-- src:1893 | of directors under subsection (3)(b), the broadcasting company must
-- src:1894 | immediately remove the person from such office.
@ref s 33(4) (src:1891-1894)
GIVEN `the Authority does not approve the appointment under subsection (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(4) the company must immediately remove the person from office` MEANS
    IF `the Authority does not approve the appointment under subsection (3)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1896 | (5) Any broadcasting company which contravenes this section shall
-- src:1897 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:1898 | exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:1899 | further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:1900 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 33(5) (guilt) (src:1896-1900)
GIVEN `the broadcasting company contravenes the section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(5) the broadcasting company is guilty of an offence` MEANS `the broadcasting company contravenes the section`

-- src:1896 | (5) Any broadcasting company which contravenes this section shall
-- src:1897 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:1898 | exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:1899 | further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:1900 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 33(5) (punishment) (src:1896-1900)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 33(5) the punishment on conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 50000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is provided`
                  , `daily fine` IS `a further fine not exceeding, per day or part of a day after conviction` 5000
                  , `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

-- src:1902 | (6) This section has effect despite the provisions of any other
-- src:1903 | written law or of the memorandum or articles of association, or other
-- src:1904 | constitution, of a broadcasting company.
@ref s 33(6) (src:1902-1904)
GIVEN `another written law or the memorandum, articles or other constitution of the company provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(6) the section has effect despite that other provision` MEANS TRUE

-- src:1906 | (7) In this section —
-- src:1908 | “chief executive officer”, in relation to a broadcasting company,
-- src:1909 | means any person, by whatever name described, who is —
-- src:1911 | (a) in the direct employment of, or acting for or by
-- src:1912 | arrangement with, the broadcasting company; and
-- src:1914 | (b) principally responsible for the management and
-- src:1915 | conduct of any type of business of the broadcasting
-- src:1916 | company in Singapore,
-- src:1921 | and includes any person for the time being performing all or
-- src:1922 | any of the functions or duties of a chief executive officer;
@ref s 33(7) chapeau and "chief executive officer" (src:1906-1922)
GIVEN `the person is in the direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the broadcasting company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is principally responsible for the management and conduct of any type of business of the company in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is for the time being performing all or any of the functions or duties of a chief executive officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(7) the person is the chief executive officer of the broadcasting company` MEANS
    (`the person is in the direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the broadcasting company` AND `the person is principally responsible for the management and conduct of any type of business of the company in Singapore`) OR `the person is for the time being performing all or any of the functions or duties of a chief executive officer`

-- src:1924 | “director” has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the
-- src:1925 | Companies Act 1967.
@ref s 33(7) "director" (src:1924-1925)
GIVEN `it is a director within the meaning of section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(7) the person is a director` MEANS `it is a director within the meaning of section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967`

§ `34. Application and interpretation of this section and sections 35 to 42`

-- src:1930 | 34.—(1) This section and sections 35 to 42 apply to, and in relation
-- src:1931 | to, all individuals whether resident in Singapore or not and whether
-- src:1932 | citizens of Singapore or not, and to all bodies corporate or
-- src:1933 | unincorporate, whether incorporated or carrying on business in
-- src:1934 | Singapore or not.
@ref s 34(1) (src:1930-1934)
GIVEN `it is an individual, whether resident in Singapore or not and whether a citizen of Singapore or not, or a body corporate or unincorporate, whether incorporated or carrying on business in Singapore or not` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(1) sections 34 to 42 apply to and in relation to it` MEANS
    `it is an individual, whether resident in Singapore or not and whether a citizen of Singapore or not, or a body corporate or unincorporate, whether incorporated or carrying on business in Singapore or not`

-- src:1938 | “arrangement” includes any formal or informal scheme,
-- src:1939 | arrangement or understanding, and any trust whether
-- src:1940 | express or implied;
@ref s 34(2) "arrangement" (src:1938-1940)
GIVEN `it is a formal or informal scheme, arrangement or understanding, or a trust express or implied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(2) arrangement includes this` MEANS
    IF `it is a formal or informal scheme, arrangement or understanding, or a trust express or implied` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1942 | “share” includes stock except where a distinction between stock
-- src:1943 | and shares is expressed or implied;
@ref s 34(2) "share" (src:1942-1943)
GIVEN `it is stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a distinction between stock and shares is expressed or implied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(2) share includes this stock` MEANS
    IF `it is stock` AND (NOT `a distinction between stock and shares is expressed or implied`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1945 | “substantial shareholder” has the meaning given by section 81 of
-- src:1946 | the Companies Act 1967, with the reference to a company in
-- src:1947 | the definition replaced with a reference to a VCC where the
-- src:1948 | entity concerned is a VCC;
@ref s 34(2) "substantial shareholder" (src:1945-1948)
-- Borrowed from section 81 of the Companies Act 1967 (with a VCC in place of a company where the entity is a VCC): asked as a fact.
GIVEN `it is a substantial shareholder within the meaning of section 81 of the Companies Act 1967, read with a VCC for the company where the entity concerned is a VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(2) the person is a substantial shareholder` MEANS
    `it is a substantial shareholder within the meaning of section 81 of the Companies Act 1967, read with a VCC for the company where the entity concerned is a VCC`

-- src:1952 | “voting share” has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the
-- src:1953 | Companies Act 1967.
@ref s 34(2) "voting share" (src:1952-1953)
GIVEN `it is a voting share within the meaning of section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(2) the share is a voting share` MEANS `it is a voting share within the meaning of section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967`

-- src:1955 | (3) In determining whether a person is a substantial shareholder of a
-- src:1956 | VCC that is an umbrella VCC for the purposes of the definition of
-- src:1957 | “substantial shareholder” in subsection (2), a reference in that
-- src:1958 | definition to voting shares in a VCC is to voting shares that are issued
-- src:1959 | in respect of one or more sub‑funds of the umbrella VCC.
@ref s 34(3) (src:1955-1959)
GIVEN `the VCC is an umbrella VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(3) the voting shares counted are those issued in respect of one or more sub-funds of the umbrella VCC` MEANS
    IF `the VCC is an umbrella VCC` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `35. Control of substantial shareholdings in broadcasting companies`

-- src:1969 | 35.—(1) A person must not, on or after 2 September 2002, become
-- src:1970 | a substantial shareholder of a broadcasting company without first
-- src:1971 | obtaining the approval of the Minister.
@ref s 35(1) (src:1969-1971)
GIVEN `the person becomes a substantial shareholder of a broadcasting company on or after 2 September 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person first obtained the approval of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(1) the person has contravened the subsection` MEANS
    `the person becomes a substantial shareholder of a broadcasting company on or after 2 September 2002` AND (NOT `the person first obtained the approval of the Minister`)

-- src:1973 | (2) Subject to section 37(4), a person who, immediately before
-- src:1974 | 2 September 2002, is a substantial shareholder of a broadcasting
-- src:1975 | company must not continue to be a substantial shareholder unless the
-- src:1976 | person has, within 6 months after 2 September 2002 or any longer
-- src:1977 | period that the Minister may allow, applied to the Minister for
-- src:1978 | approval to continue to be a substantial shareholder.
@ref s 35(2) (src:1973-1978)
GIVEN `the person was a substantial shareholder of a broadcasting company immediately before 2 September 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person applied to the Minister for approval within 6 months after 2 September 2002 or any longer period the Minister allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 37(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(2) the person may continue to be a substantial shareholder` MEANS
    IF `the person was a substantial shareholder of a broadcasting company immediately before 2 September 2002` AND (NOT `section 37(4) applies`) THEN JUST `the person applied to the Minister for approval within 6 months after 2 September 2002 or any longer period the Minister allowed` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1980 | (3) A person must not, on or after 2 September 2002, enter into any
-- src:1981 | agreement or arrangement, whether oral or in writing and whether
-- src:1982 | express or implied, to act together with any other person with respect
-- src:1983 | to the acquisition, holding or disposal of, or the exercise of rights in
-- src:1984 | relation to, their interests in voting shares of an aggregate of more
-- src:1985 | than 5% of the total votes attached to all voting shares in a
-- src:1986 | broadcasting company without first obtaining the approval of the
-- src:1987 | Minister.
@ref s 35(3) (src:1980-1987)
GIVEN `the person enters on or after 2 September 2002 into an agreement or arrangement to act together with another person about interests in voting shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the percentage of the total votes of all voting shares in the broadcasting company that those interests make up` IS A NUMBER
      `the person first obtained the approval of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(3) the person has contravened the subsection` MEANS
    `the person enters on or after 2 September 2002 into an agreement or arrangement to act together with another person about interests in voting shares` AND `the percentage of the total votes of all voting shares in the broadcasting company that those interests make up` ABOVE 5 AND (NOT `the person first obtained the approval of the Minister`)

-- src:1989 | (3A) In subsection (3), where the broadcasting company concerned
-- src:1990 | is a broadcasting holding company that is an umbrella VCC whose
-- src:1991 | shareholding in or control of a company which holds a relevant
-- src:1992 | licence by virtue of which that company is a subsidiary of the
-- src:1993 | umbrella VCC, is attributable to one or more of its sub‑funds, the
-- src:1994 | reference to the voting shares in a broadcasting company is to the
-- src:1995 | voting shares in the umbrella VCC that are issued in respect of that
-- src:1996 | sub‑fund or those sub‑funds.
@ref s 35(3A) (src:1989-1996)
GIVEN `the broadcasting company is a broadcasting holding company that is an umbrella VCC whose holding in a licensed subsidiary is attributable to sub-funds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(3A) the reference to voting shares in subsection (3) is to the voting shares in the umbrella VCC issued in respect of those sub-funds` MEANS
    IF `the broadcasting company is a broadcasting holding company that is an umbrella VCC whose holding in a licensed subsidiary is attributable to sub-funds` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2000 | (4) Subject to section 37(4), a person who, at any time before
-- src:2001 | 2 September 2002, has entered into any agreement or arrangement
-- src:2002 | mentioned in subsection (3) must not continue to be a party to the
-- src:2003 | agreement or arrangement unless the person has, within 6 months
-- src:2004 | after 2 September 2002 or any longer period that the Minister may
-- src:2005 | allow, applied to the Minister for approval to continue to be a party to
-- src:2006 | the agreement or arrangement.
@ref s 35(4) (src:2000-2006)
GIVEN `the person had before 2 September 2002 entered into an agreement or arrangement mentioned in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person applied to the Minister for approval within 6 months after 2 September 2002 or any longer period the Minister allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 37(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(4) the person may continue to be a party to the agreement or arrangement` MEANS
    IF `the person had before 2 September 2002 entered into an agreement or arrangement mentioned in subsection (3)` AND (NOT `section 37(4) applies`) THEN JUST `the person applied to the Minister for approval within 6 months after 2 September 2002 or any longer period the Minister allowed` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2011 | (5) For the purposes of this section, a person has an interest in any
-- src:2012 | share if —
-- src:2014 | (a) the person is deemed to have an interest in that share under
-- src:2015 | section 7 of the Companies Act 1967; or
-- src:2017 | (b) the person otherwise has a legal or an equitable interest in
-- src:2018 | that share except for any interest that is to be disregarded
-- src:2019 | under section 7 of the Companies Act 1967.
@ref s 35(5) (src:2011-2019)
GIVEN `the person is deemed to have an interest in the share under section 7 of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person otherwise has a legal or an equitable interest in the share, other than an interest to be disregarded under section 7 of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(5) the person has an interest in the share` MEANS
    `the person is deemed to have an interest in the share under section 7 of the Companies Act 1967` OR `the person otherwise has a legal or an equitable interest in the share, other than an interest to be disregarded under section 7 of the Companies Act 1967`

-- src:2021 | (6) The application of subsection (5) in relation to any share in a
-- src:2022 | VCC is subject to the following modifications:
-- src:2024 | (a) subsection (3) of section 7 of the Companies Act 1967 does
-- src:2025 | not apply;
-- src:2027 | (b) paragraph (ca) of section 7(9) of the Companies Act 1967
-- src:2028 | does not apply;
-- src:2030 | (c) a book-entry security is treated as an interest in a share;
-- src:2032 | (d) a person that is a subsidiary of a VCC does not have an
-- src:2033 | interest in the shares of the VCC by reason only that that
-- src:2034 | interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the
-- src:2035 | subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act.
@ref s 35(6) (src:2021-2035)
GIVEN `the share is in a VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a book-entry security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(6) the book-entry security is treated as an interest in a share` MEANS
    IF `the share is in a VCC` AND `it is a book-entry security` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Modification (a): subsection (3) of section 7 of the Companies Act 1967 does not apply to a share in a VCC.
GIVEN `the share is in a VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(6)(a) subsection (3) of section 7 of the Companies Act 1967 applies in applying subsection (5) to the share` MEANS
    IF `the share is in a VCC` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Modification (a): paragraph (ca) of section 7(9) of the Companies Act 1967 does not apply to a share in a VCC.
GIVEN `the share is in a VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(6)(b) paragraph (ca) of section 7(9) of the Companies Act 1967 applies in applying it to the share` MEANS
    IF `the share is in a VCC` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Modification: a subsidiary of a VCC does not have an interest in the shares of the VCC by reason only that the interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act.
GIVEN `the share is in a VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a subsidiary of the VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is the only reason it is said to have an interest in the shares of the VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(6)(d) the subsidiary of a VCC has an interest in the shares of the VCC` MEANS
    IF `the share is in a VCC` AND `the person is a subsidiary of the VCC` AND `the interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act` AND `that is the only reason it is said to have an interest in the shares of the VCC` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `36. Control of shareholdings and voting power in broadcasting companies`

-- src:2042 | 36.—(1) A person must not, on or after 2 September 2002,
-- src:2043 | become —
-- src:2045 | (a) a 12% controller; or
-- src:2047 | (b) an indirect controller,
-- src:2049 | of a broadcasting company without first obtaining the approval of the
-- src:2050 | Minister.
@ref s 36(1) (src:2042-2050)
GIVEN `the person becomes a 12% controller or an indirect controller of a broadcasting company on or after 2 September 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person first obtained the approval of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(1) the person has contravened the subsection` MEANS
    `the person becomes a 12% controller or an indirect controller of a broadcasting company on or after 2 September 2002` AND (NOT `the person first obtained the approval of the Minister`)

-- src:2052 | (2) Subject to section 37(4), a person who, immediately before
-- src:2053 | 2 September 2002, is —
-- src:2055 | (a) a 12% controller; or
-- src:2057 | (b) an indirect controller,
-- src:2062 | of a broadcasting company must not continue to be such a controller
-- src:2063 | unless the person has, within 6 months after 2 September 2002 or any
-- src:2064 | longer period that the Minister may allow, applied to the Minister for
-- src:2065 | approval to continue to be such a controller.
@ref s 36(2) (src:2052-2065)
GIVEN `the person was a 12% controller or an indirect controller immediately before 2 September 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person applied to the Minister for approval within 6 months after 2 September 2002 or any longer period the Minister allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 37(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(2) the person may continue to be such a controller` MEANS
    IF `the person was a 12% controller or an indirect controller immediately before 2 September 2002` AND (NOT `section 37(4) applies`) THEN JUST `the person applied to the Minister for approval within 6 months after 2 September 2002 or any longer period the Minister allowed` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2067 | (3) In subsections (1)(a) and (2)(a), “12% controller” means a
-- src:2068 | person who alone or together with the person’s associates —
-- src:2070 | (a) holds at least 12% of the shares in the broadcasting
-- src:2071 | company; or
-- src:2073 | (b) is in a position to control voting power of at least 12% in
-- src:2074 | the broadcasting company.
@ref s 36(3) "12% controller" (src:2067-2074)
GIVEN `the percentage of the shares in the broadcasting company the person, alone or together with the person's associates, holds` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the voting power in the broadcasting company the person, alone or together with associates, is in a position to control` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(3) the person is a 12% controller` MEANS
    `the percentage of the shares in the broadcasting company the person, alone or together with the person's associates, holds` AT LEAST 12 OR `the percentage of the voting power in the broadcasting company the person, alone or together with associates, is in a position to control` AT LEAST 12

-- src:2076 | (3A) In subsection (3), where the broadcasting company concerned
-- src:2077 | is a broadcasting holding company that is an umbrella VCC whose
-- src:2078 | holding in or control of a company which holds a relevant licence by
-- src:2079 | virtue of which that company is a subsidiary of the umbrella VCC, is
-- src:2080 | attributable to one or more of its sub‑funds —
-- src:2082 | (a) the reference to the shares in a broadcasting company is to
-- src:2083 | the shares in the umbrella VCC that are issued in respect of
-- src:2084 | that sub‑fund or those sub‑funds; and
-- src:2086 | (b) the reference to voting power in a broadcasting company is
-- src:2087 | to the voting power in the umbrella VCC that is exercisable
-- src:2088 | in respect of that sub‑fund or those sub‑funds.
@ref s 36(3A) (src:2076-2088)
GIVEN `the broadcasting company is a broadcasting holding company that is an umbrella VCC whose holding in a licensed subsidiary is attributable to sub-funds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(3A) the shares and voting power referred to are those of the umbrella VCC in respect of those sub-funds` MEANS
    IF `the broadcasting company is a broadcasting holding company that is an umbrella VCC whose holding in a licensed subsidiary is attributable to sub-funds` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2092 | (4) For the purposes of subsections (3) and (3A) —
-- src:2094 | (a) a person holds a share if —
-- src:2096 | (i) the person is deemed to have an interest in that share
-- src:2097 | under section 7(6) to (10) of the Companies
-- src:2098 | Act 1967; or
-- src:2100 | (ii) the person otherwise has a legal or an equitable
-- src:2101 | interest in that share except for any interest that is to
-- src:2102 | be disregarded under section 7(6) to (10) of the
-- src:2103 | Companies Act 1967;
@ref s 36(4) chapeau and (a) (src:2092-2103)
GIVEN `the person is deemed to have an interest in the share under section 7(6) to (10) of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person otherwise has a legal or an equitable interest in the share, other than an interest to be disregarded under section 7(6) to (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(4)(a) the person holds the share` MEANS
    `the person is deemed to have an interest in the share under section 7(6) to (10) of the Companies Act 1967` OR `the person otherwise has a legal or an equitable interest in the share, other than an interest to be disregarded under section 7(6) to (10)`

-- src:2105 | (b) a reference to the control of a percentage of the voting
-- src:2106 | power in a broadcasting company is a reference to the
-- src:2107 | control, whether direct or indirect, of that percentage of the
-- src:2112 | total number of votes that might be cast in a general
-- src:2113 | meeting of the broadcasting company; and
@ref s 36(4)(b) (src:2105-2113)
GIVEN `the control, direct or indirect, is of that percentage of the total number of votes that might be cast in a general meeting of the broadcasting company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(4)(b) the reference to control of a percentage of the voting power is satisfied` MEANS
    `the control, direct or indirect, is of that percentage of the total number of votes that might be cast in a general meeting of the broadcasting company`

-- src:2115 | (c) a person (A) is an associate of another person (B) if —
-- src:2117 | (i) A is the spouse or a parent, step-parent or remoter
-- src:2118 | lineal ancestor, or a son, stepson, daughter,
-- src:2119 | stepdaughter or remoter issue, or a brother or
-- src:2120 | sister, of B;
-- src:2122 | (ii) A is a corporation whose directors are accustomed or
-- src:2123 | under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to
-- src:2124 | act in accordance with the directions, instructions or
-- src:2125 | wishes of B, or where B is a corporation, of the
-- src:2126 | directors of B;
-- src:2128 | (iii) B is a corporation whose directors are accustomed or
-- src:2129 | under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to
-- src:2130 | act in accordance with the directions, instructions or
-- src:2131 | wishes of A, or where A is a corporation, of the
-- src:2132 | directors of A;
-- src:2134 | (iv) A is a person who is accustomed or under an
-- src:2135 | obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in
-- src:2136 | accordance with the directions, instructions or
-- src:2137 | wishes of B;
-- src:2139 | (v) B is a person who is accustomed or under an
-- src:2140 | obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in
-- src:2141 | accordance with the directions, instructions or
-- src:2142 | wishes of A;
-- src:2144 | (vi) A is a related corporation of B;
-- src:2146 | (vii) A is a corporation in which B, alone or together with
-- src:2147 | other associates of B as described in
-- src:2148 | sub‑paragraphs (ii) to (vi), is in a position to
-- src:2149 | control at least 20% of the voting power in A;
-- src:2151 | (viii) B is a corporation in which A, alone or together with
-- src:2152 | other associates of A as described in
-- src:2153 | sub‑paragraphs (ii) to (vi), is in a position to
-- src:2154 | control at least 20% of the voting power in B; or
-- src:2159 | (ix) A is a person with whom B has an agreement or
-- src:2160 | arrangement, whether oral or in writing and whether
-- src:2161 | express or implied, to act together with respect to the
-- src:2162 | acquisition, holding or disposal of shares or other
-- src:2163 | interests in, or with respect to the exercise of their
-- src:2164 | voting power in relation to, the broadcasting
-- src:2165 | company.
@ref s 36(4)(c) "associate" (src:2115-2165)
GIVEN `A is the spouse or a parent, step-parent or remoter lineal ancestor, or a son, stepson, daughter, stepdaughter or remoter issue, or a brother or sister, of B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A is a corporation whose directors are accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of B (or of the directors of B where B is a corporation)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `B is a corporation whose directors are accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of A (or of the directors of A where A is a corporation)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A is a person who is accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `B is a person who is accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A is a related corporation of B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A is a corporation in which B, alone or together with other associates described in sub-paragraphs (ii) to (vi), can control at least 20% of the voting power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `B is a corporation in which A, alone or together with other associates described in sub-paragraphs (ii) to (vi), can control at least 20% of the voting power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A is a person with whom B has an agreement or arrangement to act together about shares or voting power in the broadcasting company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(4)(c) A is an associate of B` MEANS
    `A is the spouse or a parent, step-parent or remoter lineal ancestor, or a son, stepson, daughter, stepdaughter or remoter issue, or a brother or sister, of B`
    OR `A is a corporation whose directors are accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of B (or of the directors of B where B is a corporation)`
    OR `B is a corporation whose directors are accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of A (or of the directors of A where A is a corporation)`
    OR `A is a person who is accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of B`
    OR `B is a person who is accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of A`
    OR `A is a related corporation of B`
    OR `A is a corporation in which B, alone or together with other associates described in sub-paragraphs (ii) to (vi), can control at least 20% of the voting power`
    OR `B is a corporation in which A, alone or together with other associates described in sub-paragraphs (ii) to (vi), can control at least 20% of the voting power`
    OR `A is a person with whom B has an agreement or arrangement to act together about shares or voting power in the broadcasting company`

-- src:2169 | (4A) The application of subsection (4)(a) in relation to any share in
-- src:2170 | a VCC is subject to the following modifications:
-- src:2172 | (a) paragraph (ca) of section 7(9) of the Companies Act 1967
-- src:2173 | does not apply;
-- src:2175 | (b) a book-entry security is treated as an interest in a share;
-- src:2177 | (c) a person that is a subsidiary of a VCC does not have an
-- src:2178 | interest in the shares of the VCC by reason only that that
-- src:2179 | interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the
-- src:2180 | subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act.
@ref s 36(4A) (src:2169-2180)
GIVEN `it is a book-entry security in a VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(4A) it is treated as an interest in a share` MEANS
    IF `it is a book-entry security in a VCC` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Modification (a): paragraph (ca) of section 7(9) of the Companies Act 1967 does not apply to a share in a VCC.
GIVEN `the share is in a VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(4A)(a) paragraph (ca) of section 7(9) of the Companies Act 1967 applies in applying it to the share` MEANS
    IF `the share is in a VCC` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Modification: a subsidiary of a VCC does not have an interest in the shares of the VCC by reason only that the interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act.
GIVEN `the share is in a VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a subsidiary of the VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is the only reason it is said to have an interest in the shares of the VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(4A)(c) the subsidiary of a VCC has an interest in the shares of the VCC` MEANS
    IF `the share is in a VCC` AND `the person is a subsidiary of the VCC` AND `the interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act` AND `that is the only reason it is said to have an interest in the shares of the VCC` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2184 | (5) In subsections (1)(b) and (2)(b), “indirect controller” means any
-- src:2185 | person, whether acting alone or together with any other person and
-- src:2186 | whether with or without holding shares or controlling voting power in
-- src:2187 | a broadcasting company —
-- src:2189 | (a) in accordance with whose directions, instructions or
-- src:2190 | wishes the directors of the broadcasting company are
-- src:2191 | accustomed or under an obligation, whether formal or
-- src:2192 | informal, to act; or
-- src:2194 | (b) who is in a position to determine the policy of the
-- src:2195 | broadcasting company,
-- src:2197 | but does not include any person —
-- src:2199 | (c) who is a director or other officer of the broadcasting
-- src:2200 | company whose appointment has been approved by the
-- src:2201 | Authority; or
-- src:2203 | (d) in accordance with whose directions, instructions or
-- src:2204 | wishes the directors of the broadcasting company are
-- src:2209 | accustomed to act by reason only that they act on advice
-- src:2210 | given by the person in the person’s professional capacity.
@ref s 36(5) "indirect controller" (src:2184-2210)
GIVEN `the directors of the broadcasting company are accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the person's directions, instructions or wishes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in a position to determine the policy of the broadcasting company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or other officer whose appointment the Authority approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors are accustomed to act on the person's directions only because they act on advice the person gives in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(5) the person is an indirect controller` MEANS
    (NOT `the person is a director or other officer whose appointment the Authority approved`)
    AND (NOT `the directors are accustomed to act on the person's directions only because they act on advice the person gives in a professional capacity`)
    AND (`the directors of the broadcasting company are accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the person's directions, instructions or wishes` OR `the person is in a position to determine the policy of the broadcasting company`)

§ `37. Approval of applications`

-- src:2214 | 37.—(1) The Minister may approve an application made by any
-- src:2215 | person under section 35 or 36 if the Minister is satisfied that —
-- src:2217 | (a) the person is a fit and proper person;
-- src:2219 | (b) having regard to the person’s likely influence, the
-- src:2220 | broadcasting company will or will continue to conduct
-- src:2221 | its business prudently and comply with the provisions of
-- src:2222 | this Act; and
-- src:2224 | (c) it is in the national interest to do so.
@ref s 37(1) (src:2214-2224)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the person is a fit and proper person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that, having regard to the person's likely influence, the company will or will continue to conduct its business prudently and comply with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that it is in the national interest to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(1) the Minister may approve the application` MEANS
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person is a fit and proper person` AND `the Minister is satisfied that, having regard to the person's likely influence, the company will or will continue to conduct its business prudently and comply with this Act` AND `the Minister is satisfied that it is in the national interest to do so`

-- src:2226 | (2) Any approval under this section may be granted to any person
-- src:2227 | subject to any conditions that the Minister may determine, including
-- src:2228 | but not limited to any condition —
-- src:2230 | (a) restricting the person’s disposal or further acquisition of
-- src:2231 | shares or voting power in the broadcasting company; or
-- src:2233 | (b) restricting the person’s exercise of voting power in the
-- src:2234 | broadcasting company.
@ref s 37(2) (src:2226-2234)
GIVEN `it is a condition restricting the person's disposal or further acquisition of shares or voting power in the broadcasting company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a condition restricting the person's exercise of voting power in the broadcasting company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(2) the Minister may attach this condition to the approval` MEANS
    IF `it is a condition restricting the person's disposal or further acquisition of shares or voting power in the broadcasting company` OR `it is a condition restricting the person's exercise of voting power in the broadcasting company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2236 | (3) Any condition imposed under subsection (2) has effect despite
-- src:2237 | any of the provisions of the Companies Act 1967 or the VCC Act
-- src:2238 | (whichever is applicable) or anything contained in the memorandum
-- src:2239 | or articles of association, or other constitution, of the broadcasting
-- src:2240 | company.
@ref s 37(3) (src:2236-2240)
GIVEN `another provision of the Companies Act 1967 or the VCC Act, or the memorandum or articles or other constitution of the broadcasting company, provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(3) the condition has effect despite that provision` MEANS TRUE

-- src:2244 | (4) Where the Minister does not approve an application made by
-- src:2245 | any person under section 35(2) or (4) or 36(2), the person must,
-- src:2246 | within the time that the Minister may specify, take such steps as are
-- src:2247 | necessary —
-- src:2249 | (a) in the case of section 35(2), to cease to be a substantial
-- src:2250 | shareholder;
-- src:2252 | (b) in the case of section 35(4), to cease to be a party to the
-- src:2253 | agreement or arrangement; or
-- src:2258 | (c) in the case of section 36(2), to cease to be —
-- src:2260 | (i) a 12% controller; or
-- src:2262 | (ii) an indirect controller,
-- src:2264 | (c) as the case may be.
@ref s 37(4) (src:2244-2264)
GIVEN `the Minister does not approve an application under section 35(2) or (4) or 36(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(4) the person must within the time the Minister specifies take the necessary steps to cease to be the substantial shareholder, party or controller` MEANS
    IF `the Minister does not approve an application under section 35(2) or (4) or 36(2)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `39. Objection to existing control of broadcasting company`

-- src:2270 | 39.—(1) The Minister may serve a written notice of objection on
-- src:2271 | any person mentioned in section 35 or 36 if the Minister is satisfied
-- src:2272 | that —
-- src:2274 | (a) any condition of approval imposed on the person under
-- src:2275 | section 37(2) has not been complied with;
-- src:2277 | (b) the person ceases to be a fit and proper person;
-- src:2279 | (c) having regard to the person’s likely influence, the
-- src:2280 | broadcasting company is no longer likely to conduct its
-- src:2281 | business prudently or to comply with the provisions of this
-- src:2282 | Act;
-- src:2284 | (d) it is no longer in the national interest to allow the person to
-- src:2285 | continue to be a party to the agreement or arrangement
-- src:2286 | described in section 35(3) or (4), or to continue to be a
-- src:2287 | substantial shareholder, a 12% controller or an indirect
-- src:2288 | controller, as the case may be;
-- src:2290 | (e) the person has provided false or misleading information or
-- src:2291 | documents in connection with an application under
-- src:2292 | section 35 or 36; or
-- src:2294 | (f) the Minister would not have granted his or her approval
-- src:2295 | under section 37 had the Minister been aware, at that time,
-- src:2296 | of the circumstances relevant to the person’s application
-- src:2297 | for the approval.
@ref s 39(1) (src:2270-2297)
GIVEN `a condition of approval imposed under section 37(2) has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person ceases to be a fit and proper person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is no longer likely to conduct its business prudently or comply with this Act, having regard to the person's likely influence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is no longer in the national interest to allow the person to continue as party, substantial shareholder, 12% controller or indirect controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person provided false or misleading information or documents in connection with an application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister would not have granted approval had the Minister known the circumstances at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(1) the Minister may serve a written notice of objection on the person` MEANS
    `a condition of approval imposed under section 37(2) has not been complied with` OR `the person ceases to be a fit and proper person` OR `the company is no longer likely to conduct its business prudently or comply with this Act, having regard to the person's likely influence` OR `it is no longer in the national interest to allow the person to continue as party, substantial shareholder, 12% controller or indirect controller` OR `the person provided false or misleading information or documents in connection with an application` OR `the Minister would not have granted approval had the Minister known the circumstances at that time`

-- src:2299 | (2) Before serving a written notice of objection, the Minister must,
-- src:2300 | unless he or she decides that it is not practicable or desirable to do so,
-- src:2301 | cause to be given to the person concerned written notice of the
-- src:2302 | Minister’s intention to serve the written notice of objection,
-- src:2307 | specifying a date by which the person may make written
-- src:2308 | representations with regard to the proposed written notice of
-- src:2309 | objection.
@ref s 39(2) (src:2299-2309)
GIVEN `the Minister decides it is not practicable or desirable to give written notice of intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(2) the Minister must first give written notice of intention, specifying a date for representations` MEANS
    NOT `the Minister decides it is not practicable or desirable to give written notice of intention`

-- src:2311 | (3) Upon receiving the written representations of any person
-- src:2312 | mentioned in subsection (2), the Minister must consider the written
-- src:2313 | representations for the purpose of determining whether to issue a
-- src:2314 | written notice of objection.
@ref s 39(3) (src:2311-2314)
GIVEN `the Minister has received the written representations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(3) the Minister must consider the representations in deciding whether to issue the notice of objection` MEANS
    `the Minister has received the written representations`

-- src:2316 | (4) The Minister must, in any written notice of objection, specify a
-- src:2317 | reasonable period within which the person to be served the written
-- src:2318 | notice of objection must —
-- src:2320 | (a) take such steps as are necessary to ensure that the person
-- src:2321 | ceases to be a party to the agreement or arrangement
-- src:2322 | described in section 35(3) or (4), or ceases to be a
-- src:2323 | substantial shareholder, a 12% controller or an indirect
-- src:2324 | controller, as the case may be; or
-- src:2326 | (b) comply with any direction or restriction that the Minister
-- src:2327 | may make under section 40.
@ref s 39(4) (src:2316-2327)
GIVEN `the notice specifies a reasonable period within which the person must cease to be a party, substantial shareholder or controller, or comply with a direction or restriction under section 40` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(4) the notice of objection is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the notice specifies a reasonable period within which the person must cease to be a party, substantial shareholder or controller, or comply with a direction or restriction under section 40`

-- src:2329 | (5) Any person served with a written notice of objection under this
-- src:2330 | section must comply with the notice.
@ref s 39(5) (src:2329-2330)
GIVEN `the person has been served with a written notice of objection under the section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(5) the person must comply with the notice` MEANS
    `the person has been served with a written notice of objection under the section`

§ `40. Power to make directions`

-- src:2334 | 40.—(1) Without affecting section 41, if the Minister is satisfied
-- src:2335 | that any person has contravened section 35, 36, 37(4) or 39(5) or any
-- src:2336 | condition imposed under section 37(2), or if the Minister has served a
-- src:2337 | written notice of objection under section 39, the Minister may, by
-- src:2338 | written notice —
-- src:2340 | (a) direct the transfer or disposal of all or any of the shares in
-- src:2341 | the broadcasting company held by the person or any of the
-- src:2342 | person’s associates (called in this section the specified
-- src:2343 | shares) within such time and subject to such conditions as
-- src:2344 | the Minister considers appropriate;
-- src:2346 | (b) restrict the transfer or disposal of the specified shares; or
-- src:2348 | (c) make any other direction or restriction that the Minister
-- src:2349 | considers appropriate.
@ref s 40(1) (src:2334-2349)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the person has contravened section 35, 36, 37(4) or 39(5) or a condition under section 37(2), or has served a notice of objection under section 39` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(1) the Minister may by written notice direct a transfer or disposal of the specified shares, restrict their transfer or disposal, or make any other direction or restriction the Minister considers appropriate` MEANS
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person has contravened section 35, 36, 37(4) or 39(5) or a condition under section 37(2), or has served a notice of objection under section 39`

-- src:2354 | (2) Any person to whom a notice is served under subsection (1)
-- src:2355 | must comply with any direction or restriction that may be specified in
-- src:2356 | the notice.
@ref s 40(2) (src:2354-2356)
GIVEN `a notice has been served on the person under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(2) the person must comply with the direction or restriction specified in the notice` MEANS
    `a notice has been served on the person under subsection (1)`

-- src:2358 | (3) In the case of any direction or restriction made under
-- src:2359 | subsection (1)(a) or (b), despite any of the provisions of the
-- src:2360 | Companies Act 1967 or the VCC Act (whichever is applicable) or
-- src:2361 | anything contained in the memorandum or articles of association, or
-- src:2362 | other constitution, of the broadcasting company —
-- src:2364 | (a) no voting rights are exercisable in respect of the specified
-- src:2365 | shares unless the Minister expressly permits those rights to
-- src:2366 | be exercised;
-- src:2368 | (b) no shares of the broadcasting company are to be issued or
-- src:2369 | offered (whether by way of rights, bonus or otherwise) in
-- src:2370 | respect of the specified shares unless the Minister
-- src:2371 | expressly permits such issue or offer; and
-- src:2373 | (c) except in a liquidation of the broadcasting company, no
-- src:2374 | payment is to be made by the broadcasting company of any
-- src:2375 | amount (whether by way of dividends or otherwise) in
-- src:2376 | respect of the specified shares unless the Minister
-- src:2377 | expressly authorises such payment,
-- src:2379 | until a transfer or disposal is effected in accordance with the direction
-- src:2380 | or until the restriction on a transfer or disposal is removed, as the case
-- src:2381 | may be.
@ref s 40(3) (src:2358-2381)
-- The three limbs hold "until a transfer or disposal is effected in accordance with the direction or until the restriction on a transfer or disposal is removed".
GIVEN `a direction or restriction has been made under subsection (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a transfer or disposal has been effected in accordance with the direction, or the restriction has been removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has expressly permitted the voting rights to be exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(3)(a) voting rights are exercisable in respect of the specified shares` MEANS
    IF `a direction or restriction has been made under subsection (1)(a) or (b)` AND (NOT `a transfer or disposal has been effected in accordance with the direction, or the restriction has been removed`) THEN JUST `the Minister has expressly permitted the voting rights to be exercised` ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `a direction or restriction has been made under subsection (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a transfer or disposal has been effected in accordance with the direction, or the restriction has been removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has expressly permitted the issue or offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(3)(b) shares of the broadcasting company may be issued or offered in respect of the specified shares` MEANS
    IF `a direction or restriction has been made under subsection (1)(a) or (b)` AND (NOT `a transfer or disposal has been effected in accordance with the direction, or the restriction has been removed`) THEN JUST `the Minister has expressly permitted the issue or offer` ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `a direction or restriction has been made under subsection (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a transfer or disposal has been effected in accordance with the direction, or the restriction has been removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made in a liquidation of the broadcasting company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has expressly authorised the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(3)(c) payment may be made by the broadcasting company of an amount in respect of the specified shares` MEANS
    IF `a direction or restriction has been made under subsection (1)(a) or (b)` AND (NOT `a transfer or disposal has been effected in accordance with the direction, or the restriction has been removed`) THEN JUST (`the payment is made in a liquidation of the broadcasting company` OR `the Minister has expressly authorised the payment`) ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2385 | (4) In this section, “associate” has the meaning given by
-- src:2386 | section 36(4)(c).
@ref s 40(4) (src:2385-2386)
GIVEN `it is an associate within section 36(4)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(4) the person is an associate` MEANS `it is an associate within section 36(4)(c)`

§ `41. Offences, penalties and defences`

-- src:2390 | 41.—(1) Any person who contravenes section 35, 36(1)(a) or (2)(a)
-- src:2391 | or 37(4)(a), (b) or (c)(i) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:2392 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the case
-- src:2393 | of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for
-- src:2394 | every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:2395 | conviction.
@ref s 41(1) (guilt) (src:2390-2395)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 35, 36(1)(a) or (2)(a) or 37(4)(a), (b) or (c)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS `the person contravenes section 35, 36(1)(a) or (2)(a) or 37(4)(a), (b) or (c)(i)`

-- src:2390 | 41.—(1) Any person who contravenes section 35, 36(1)(a) or (2)(a)
-- src:2391 | or 37(4)(a), (b) or (c)(i) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:2392 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the case
-- src:2393 | of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for
-- src:2394 | every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:2395 | conviction.
@ref s 41(1) (punishment) (src:2390-2395)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 41(1) the punishment on conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 50000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is provided`
                  , `daily fine` IS `a further fine not exceeding, per day or part of a day after conviction` 5000
                  , `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

-- src:2400 | (2) Any person who contravenes section 36(1)(b) or (2)(b),
-- src:2401 | 37(4)(c)(ii), 39(5) or 40(2) or any condition imposed under
-- src:2402 | section 37(2) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:2403 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:2404 | term not exceeding 3 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:2405 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of
-- src:2406 | a day during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 41(2) (guilt) (src:2400-2406)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 36(1)(b) or (2)(b), 37(4)(c)(ii), 39(5) or 40(2) or a condition imposed under section 37(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(2) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS `the person contravenes section 36(1)(b) or (2)(b), 37(4)(c)(ii), 39(5) or 40(2) or a condition imposed under section 37(2)`

-- src:2400 | (2) Any person who contravenes section 36(1)(b) or (2)(b),
-- src:2401 | 37(4)(c)(ii), 39(5) or 40(2) or any condition imposed under
-- src:2402 | section 37(2) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:2403 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:2404 | term not exceeding 3 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:2405 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of
-- src:2406 | a day during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 41(2) (punishment) (src:2400-2406)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 41(2) the punishment on conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 50000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `imprisonment not exceeding` 36
                  , `daily fine` IS `a further fine not exceeding, per day or part of a day after conviction` 5000
                  , `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

-- src:2408 | (3) Where a person is charged with an offence in respect of a
-- src:2409 | contravention of section 35 or 36, it is a defence for the person to
-- src:2410 | prove that —
-- src:2412 | (a) the person was not aware that the person had contravened
-- src:2413 | section 35 or 36, as the case may be; and
-- src:2415 | (b) the person has, within 14 days of becoming aware that the
-- src:2416 | person had contravened section 35 or 36 (as the case may
-- src:2417 | be), notified the Minister of the contravention and, within
-- src:2418 | the time that may be determined by the Minister, taken
-- src:2419 | such actions in relation to the person’s shareholding or
-- src:2420 | control of the voting power in the broadcasting company as
-- src:2421 | the Minister may direct.
@ref s 41(3) (src:2408-2421)
GIVEN `the person was charged with an offence for a contravention of section 35 or 36` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was not aware of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person notified the Minister within 14 days of becoming aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person within the time the Minister determined took the actions the Minister directed on the shareholding or voting power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(3) the person has the defence` MEANS
    IF `the person was charged with an offence for a contravention of section 35 or 36` THEN JUST (`the person was not aware of the contravention` AND `the person notified the Minister within 14 days of becoming aware of it` AND `the person within the time the Minister determined took the actions the Minister directed on the shareholding or voting power`) ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2423 | (4) Where a person is charged with an offence in respect of a
-- src:2424 | contravention of section 36(1), it is also a defence for the person to
-- src:2425 | prove that, even though the person was aware of the contravention —
-- src:2427 | (a) the contravention occurred as a result of an increase in the
-- src:2428 | shareholding as described in section 36(4)(a) of, or in the
-- src:2429 | voting power controlled by, any of his associates described
-- src:2430 | in section 36(4)(c)(i);
-- src:2432 | (b) the person has no agreement or arrangement, whether oral
-- src:2433 | or in writing and whether express or implied, with that
-- src:2434 | associate with respect to the acquisition, holding or
-- src:2435 | disposal of shares or other interests in, or under which
-- src:2436 | they act together in exercising their voting power in
-- src:2437 | relation to, the broadcasting company; and
-- src:2439 | (c) the person has, within 14 days of the date of the
-- src:2440 | contravention, notified the Minister of the contravention
-- src:2441 | and, within the time that may be determined by the
-- src:2446 | Minister, taken such action in relation to the person’s
-- src:2447 | shareholding or control of the voting power in the
-- src:2448 | broadcasting company as the Minister may direct.
@ref s 41(4) (src:2423-2448)
GIVEN `the person was charged with an offence for a contravention of section 36(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contravention occurred as a result of an increase in the shareholding, or in the voting power controlled, of an associate described in section 36(4)(c)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has no agreement or arrangement with that associate about acquiring, holding, disposing of or voting the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person notified the Minister within 14 days of the date of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person within the time the Minister determined took the action the Minister directed on the shareholding or voting power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(4) the person has the further defence even though aware` MEANS
    IF `the person was charged with an offence for a contravention of section 36(1)` THEN JUST (`the contravention occurred as a result of an increase in the shareholding, or in the voting power controlled, of an associate described in section 36(4)(c)(i)` AND `the person has no agreement or arrangement with that associate about acquiring, holding, disposing of or voting the shares` AND `the person notified the Minister within 14 days of the date of the contravention` AND `the person within the time the Minister determined took the action the Minister directed on the shareholding or voting power`) ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2450 | (5) Except as provided in subsections (3) and (4), it is not a defence
-- src:2451 | for a person charged with an offence in respect of a contravention of
-- src:2452 | section 35 or 36 to prove that the person did not intend to or did not
-- src:2453 | knowingly contravene section 35 or 36, as the case may be.
@ref s 41(5) (src:2450-2453)
GIVEN `the person proves the person did not intend to or did not knowingly contravene` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the defence under subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(5) the person has a defence in proving that the person did not intend to or did not knowingly contravene section 35 or 36` MEANS
    `the person has the defence under subsection (3) or (4)`

§ `42. Power to obtain information`

-- src:2457 | 42.—(1) The Authority may, by written notice, direct any
-- src:2458 | broadcasting company to obtain from any of its shareholders and
-- src:2459 | to transmit to the Authority information —
-- src:2461 | (a) as to whether that shareholder holds any share in the
-- src:2462 | broadcasting company as beneficial owner or as trustee;
-- src:2463 | and
-- src:2465 | (b) if the shareholder holds the share as trustee, to indicate, so
-- src:2466 | far as the shareholder can, the person for whom the
-- src:2467 | shareholder holds the share (either by name or by other
-- src:2468 | particulars sufficient to enable that person to be identified)
-- src:2469 | and the nature of that person’s interest,
-- src:2471 | and the broadcasting company must comply with that direction
-- src:2472 | within the time that may be specified in the notice.
@ref s 42(1) (src:2457-2472)
GIVEN `the Authority has by written notice directed the broadcasting company to obtain from its shareholders and transmit information about beneficial ownership or trusteeship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 42(1) the broadcasting company must comply within the time specified in the notice` MEANS
    `the Authority has by written notice directed the broadcasting company to obtain from its shareholders and transmit information about beneficial ownership or trusteeship`

-- src:2474 | (2) The Authority may, by written notice, require any shareholder
-- src:2475 | of a broadcasting company, or any person who appears from the
-- src:2476 | information provided to the Authority under subsection (1) or this
-- src:2477 | subsection to have an interest in any share in a broadcasting company,
-- src:2478 | to inform the Authority —
-- src:2480 | (a) whether the person holds that interest as beneficial owner
-- src:2481 | or as trustee, and if the person holds the interest as trustee,
-- src:2482 | to indicate, so far as he or she can, the person for whom he
-- src:2483 | or she holds the interest (either by name or by other
-- src:2484 | particulars sufficient to enable that person to be identified)
-- src:2485 | and the nature of his or her interest; or
-- src:2487 | (b) whether any share or any voting right attached to the share
-- src:2488 | is the subject of an agreement or arrangement described in
-- src:2493 | section 35(3) or (4) or 36(4)(c)(ix), and if so, to give
-- src:2494 | particulars of the agreement or arrangement and the parties
-- src:2495 | to it,
-- src:2497 | and the person must comply with the notice within the time that may
-- src:2498 | be specified in the notice.
@ref s 42(2) (src:2474-2498)
GIVEN `the Authority has by written notice required the shareholder, or a person who appears to have an interest in a share, to inform it whether the interest is held as beneficial owner or trustee, or whether a share or voting right is the subject of an agreement or arrangement described in section 35(3) or (4) or 36(4)(c)(ix)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 42(2) the person must comply with the notice within the time specified` MEANS
    `the Authority has by written notice required the shareholder, or a person who appears to have an interest in a share, to inform it whether the interest is held as beneficial owner or trustee, or whether a share or voting right is the subject of an agreement or arrangement described in section 35(3) or (4) or 36(4)(c)(ix)`

-- src:2500 | (3) Any person who —
-- src:2502 | (a) fails to comply with a notice under this section; or
-- src:2504 | (b) in purported compliance of the notice, knowingly or
