                  , `daily fine` IS `a further fine not exceeding, per day or part of a day after conviction` 5000
                  , `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

§ `43. Funds from foreign source for purposes of certain broadcasting service`

-- src:2517 | 43.—(1) Subject to this section, a person must not, without the prior
-- src:2518 | consent of the Authority, receive any fund from any foreign source
-- src:2519 | for the purposes of financing, directly or indirectly, wholly or partly,
-- src:2520 | any broadcasting service owned or operated by any broadcasting
-- src:2521 | company.
@ref s 43(1) (src:2517-2521)
GIVEN `the person receives a fund from a foreign source for the purposes of financing, directly or indirectly, wholly or partly, a broadcasting service owned or operated by a broadcasting company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority gave its prior consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43(1) the person has contravened the subsection` MEANS
    `the person receives a fund from a foreign source for the purposes of financing, directly or indirectly, wholly or partly, a broadcasting service owned or operated by a broadcasting company` AND (NOT `the Authority gave its prior consent`)

-- src:2523 | (2) The Authority may grant its consent under subsection (1) if it is
-- src:2524 | satisfied, on any information that it may require to be provided to it,
-- src:2525 | that the fund from a foreign source is intended for bona fide
-- src:2526 | commercial purposes.
@ref s 43(2) (src:2523-2526)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied, on the information it required, that the fund is intended for bona fide commercial purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43(2) the Authority may grant its consent` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied, on the information it required, that the fund is intended for bona fide commercial purposes`

-- src:2528 | (3) Despite subsection (1), where any fund from a foreign source is
-- src:2529 | sent to a person without the person’s prior knowledge, consent or
-- src:2530 | solicitation and the fund is intended for or given by the sender for any
-- src:2531 | purpose mentioned in that subsection, that person must, within 7 days
-- src:2532 | of receiving the fund, report to the Authority the circumstances and
-- src:2533 | particulars of the receipt of the fund and the purpose for which the
-- src:2534 | fund was received.
@ref s 43(3) (src:2528-2534)
GIVEN `a fund from a foreign source was sent to the person without the person's prior knowledge, consent or solicitation, for a purpose in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days since the person received the fund` IS A NUMBER
      `the person has reported to the Authority the circumstances and particulars of the receipt and the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(3) the person has complied with the duty to report within 7 days` MEANS
    IF `a fund from a foreign source was sent to the person without the person's prior knowledge, consent or solicitation, for a purpose in subsection (1)` THEN JUST (`the person has reported to the Authority the circumstances and particulars of the receipt and the purpose` AND `the days since the person received the fund` AT MOST 7) ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2539 | (4) Where any fund from a foreign source has been received by a
-- src:2540 | person for any purpose mentioned in subsection (1) and the Authority
-- src:2541 | refuses to grant consent to retain the fund, the person must, within the
-- src:2542 | time that is specified by the Authority, return the fund to its sender or,
-- src:2543 | if the sender cannot be traced, donate the fund to any charity specified
-- src:2544 | by the Authority.
@ref s 43(4) (src:2539-2544)
GIVEN `the Authority refuses to grant consent to retain the fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person returned the fund to its sender within the time the Authority specified, or, if the sender cannot be traced, donated it to the charity the Authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(4) the person has complied` MEANS
    IF `the Authority refuses to grant consent to retain the fund` THEN JUST `the person returned the fund to its sender within the time the Authority specified, or, if the sender cannot be traced, donated it to the charity the Authority specified` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2546 | (5) Any employee of a broadcasting company who, having received
-- src:2547 | any fund from a foreign source for the broadcasting of any item or
-- src:2548 | programme or for adopting a particular line or bias in respect of any
-- src:2549 | item or programme, fails to report in writing, within 7 days of
-- src:2550 | receiving the fund, to the company’s chief executive shall be guilty of
-- src:2551 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to the same penalty
-- src:2552 | prescribed by subsection (8).
@ref s 43(5) (src:2546-2552)
GIVEN `the person is an employee of a broadcasting company who received a fund from a foreign source for the broadcasting of an item or programme or for adopting a particular line or bias` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee reported in writing to the company's chief executive within 7 days of receiving the fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43(5) the employee is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person is an employee of a broadcasting company who received a fund from a foreign source for the broadcasting of an item or programme or for adopting a particular line or bias` AND (NOT `the employee reported in writing to the company's chief executive within 7 days of receiving the fund`)

-- src:2554 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (5), any fund received from
-- src:2555 | outside Singapore by an employee is presumed to be from a foreign
-- src:2556 | source until the contrary is proved.
@ref s 43(6) (src:2554-2556)
GIVEN `the fund was received from outside Singapore by an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(6) the fund is presumed to be from a foreign source until the contrary is proved` MEANS
    IF `the fund was received from outside Singapore by an employee` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2558 | (7) Nothing in this section applies to any dealing by any person in
-- src:2559 | the shares of a broadcasting company quoted on a stock exchange in
-- src:2560 | Singapore.
@ref s 43(7) (src:2558-2560)
GIVEN `it is a dealing by a person in the shares of a broadcasting company quoted on a stock exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43(7) the section applies to the dealing` MEANS
    NOT `it is a dealing by a person in the shares of a broadcasting company quoted on a stock exchange in Singapore`

-- src:2562 | (8) Any person who contravenes subsection (1), (3) or (4) shall be
-- src:2563 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:2564 | exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:2565 | 3 years or to both, and the court may, in addition to any other penalty
-- src:2566 | that it may impose, order the forfeiture to the Authority of any fund
-- src:2567 | which is the subject of the charge.
@ref s 43(8) (guilt) (src:2562-2567)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (1), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43(8) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS `the person contravenes subsection (1), (3) or (4)`

-- src:2562 | (8) Any person who contravenes subsection (1), (3) or (4) shall be
-- src:2563 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:2564 | exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:2565 | 3 years or to both, and the court may, in addition to any other penalty
-- src:2566 | that it may impose, order the forfeiture to the Authority of any fund
-- src:2567 | which is the subject of the charge.
@ref s 43(8) (punishment) (src:2562-2567)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 43(8) the punishment on conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 50000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `imprisonment not exceeding` 36
                  , `daily fine` IS `no further daily fine is provided`
                  , `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

-- src:2562 | (8) Any person who contravenes subsection (1), (3) or (4) shall be
-- src:2563 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:2564 | exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:2565 | 3 years or to both, and the court may, in addition to any other penalty
-- src:2566 | that it may impose, order the forfeiture to the Authority of any fund
-- src:2567 | which is the subject of the charge.
@ref s 43(8) (forfeiture of the fund, in addition) (src:2562-2567)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(8) the court may in addition order the forfeiture to the Authority of any fund which is the subject of the charge` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection (8)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2569 | (9) In this section and section 44 —
-- src:2571 | “foreign source” includes —
-- src:2573 | (a) the government of a country outside Singapore or the
-- src:2574 | agent of that government, whether resident in
-- src:2575 | Singapore or otherwise;
-- src:2577 | (b) any company, association or society incorporated or
-- src:2578 | constituted under any law in force outside Singapore,
-- src:2579 | whether or not it has a branch office or place of
-- src:2580 | business in Singapore;
-- src:2585 | (c) any person who is not a citizen of Singapore, whether
-- src:2586 | or not he or she is resident in Singapore;
@ref s 43(9) chapeau and "foreign source", paragraphs (a) to (c) (src:2569-2586)
GIVEN `it is the government of a country outside Singapore or the agent of that government, whether resident in Singapore or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a company, association or society incorporated or constituted under a law in force outside Singapore, whether or not it has a branch office or place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a person who is not a citizen of Singapore, whether or not resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(9) foreign source includes this person` MEANS
    IF `it is the government of a country outside Singapore or the agent of that government, whether resident in Singapore or otherwise` OR `it is a company, association or society incorporated or constituted under a law in force outside Singapore, whether or not it has a branch office or place of business in Singapore` OR `it is a person who is not a citizen of Singapore, whether or not resident in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Paragraph (d) is printed as "(d) any - (i) body corporate ...; or (ii) unincorporated association ..." followed by a second paragraph lettered (d),
-- "as the Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, declare to be a foreign source".
-- Read with the second (d) as the closing words of the first, a Singapore body with a non-citizen member or director is a foreign source only if the Minister declares it (reading A).
-- Read as two separate paragraphs, the body is a foreign source outright and the Minister's declaration is an extra route (reading B).
-- The two readings differ for a Singapore body that is not declared (F-BA-06), so the encoding does not choose: that case answers NOTHING.
-- src:2588 | (d) any —
-- src:2590 | (i) body corporate formed or incorporated in
-- src:2591 | Singapore, one or more of whose members or
-- src:2592 | directors are not citizens of Singapore, or in the
-- src:2593 | case of a member being another company,
-- src:2594 | where one or more of the members or directors
-- src:2595 | of that company are not citizens of Singapore;
-- src:2596 | or
-- src:2598 | (ii) unincorporated association or body constituted
-- src:2599 | under any law in force in Singapore, one or
-- src:2600 | more of whose members or directors are not
-- src:2601 | citizens of Singapore, or in the case of a
-- src:2602 | member being another company, where one or
-- src:2603 | more of the members or directors of that
-- src:2604 | company are not citizens of Singapore,
-- src:2606 | (d) as the Minister may, by notification in the Gazette,
-- src:2607 | declare to be a foreign source; or
@ref s 43(9)(d) bodies formed in Singapore with a non-citizen member or director, "as the Minister may declare" (F-BA-06) (src:2588-2607)
GIVEN `it is a body corporate formed or incorporated in Singapore, or an unincorporated association or body constituted under a law in force in Singapore, one or more of whose members or directors (or those of a member company) are not citizens of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette declared it to be a foreign source` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(9) foreign source includes this Singapore body` MEANS
    IF `it is a body corporate formed or incorporated in Singapore, or an unincorporated association or body constituted under a law in force in Singapore, one or more of whose members or directors (or those of a member company) are not citizens of Singapore` AND `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette declared it to be a foreign source` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2609 | (e) any other source outside Singapore that the Minister
-- src:2610 | may, by notification in the Gazette, declare to be a
-- src:2611 | foreign source;
@ref s 43(9)(e) "any other source outside Singapore that the Minister may declare to be a foreign source" (src:2609-2611)
GIVEN `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette declared it to be a foreign source` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(9) foreign source includes this declared source` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette declared it to be a foreign source` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2613 | “fund” means money, securities, movable or immovable
-- src:2614 | property or other valuable consideration;
@ref s 43(9) "fund" (src:2613-2614)
GIVEN `it is money, securities, movable or immovable property or other valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43(9) the thing is a fund` MEANS `it is money, securities, movable or immovable property or other valuable consideration`

-- src:2616 | “fund from a foreign source” includes any fund provided by a
-- src:2617 | foreign source indirectly through any agent of the foreign
-- src:2618 | source.
@ref s 43(9) "fund from a foreign source" (src:2616-2618)
GIVEN `it is a fund provided by a foreign source indirectly through an agent of the foreign source` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(9) fund from a foreign source includes this fund` MEANS
    IF `it is a fund provided by a foreign source indirectly through an agent of the foreign source` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `44. Broadcasting company owned by foreign source`

-- src:2622 | 44.—(1) A company must not, unless the Minister otherwise
-- src:2623 | approves, be granted or hold a relevant licence if the Minister is
-- src:2624 | satisfied that —
-- src:2626 | (a) any foreign source, alone or together with one or more
-- src:2627 | other foreign sources —
-- src:2632 | (i) holds at least 49% of the shares in the company or its
-- src:2633 | holding company; or
-- src:2635 | (ii) is in a position to control voting power of at least
-- src:2636 | 49% in the company or its holding company; or
-- src:2638 | (b) all or a majority of the persons having the direction, control
-- src:2639 | or management of the company or its holding company
-- src:2640 | are —
-- src:2642 | (i) appointed by; or
-- src:2644 | (ii) accustomed or under an obligation, whether formal
-- src:2645 | or informal, to act in accordance with the directions,
-- src:2646 | instructions or wishes of,
-- src:2648 | (b) any foreign source, whether acting alone or together with
-- src:2649 | one or more other foreign sources.
@ref s 44(1) (src:2622-2649)
-- Read as: a company must not be granted or hold a relevant licence, unless the Minister otherwise approves, if the Minister is satisfied that (a) foreign sources hold or control at least 49%, or (b) all or a majority of the persons directing it are appointed by, or accustomed to act for, a foreign source (see F-BA-07 on the printed lettering).
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that foreign sources, alone or together, hold at least 49% of the shares in the company or its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that foreign sources, alone or together, are in a position to control at least 49% of the voting power in the company or its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that all or a majority of the persons having the direction, control or management of the company or its holding company are appointed by, or accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of, a foreign source` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has otherwise approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(1) the company must not be granted or hold a relevant licence` MEANS
    (NOT `the Minister has otherwise approved`) AND (`the Minister is satisfied that foreign sources, alone or together, hold at least 49% of the shares in the company or its holding company` OR `the Minister is satisfied that foreign sources, alone or together, are in a position to control at least 49% of the voting power in the company or its holding company` OR `the Minister is satisfied that all or a majority of the persons having the direction, control or management of the company or its holding company are appointed by, or accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of, a foreign source`)

-- src:2651 | (1A) In subsection (1), where the holding company concerned is an
-- src:2652 | umbrella VCC whose holding in or control of the company by virtue
-- src:2653 | of which that company is a subsidiary of the umbrella VCC, is
-- src:2654 | attributable to one or more of its sub‑funds —
-- src:2656 | (a) the reference to the shares in the holding company is to the
-- src:2657 | shares in the umbrella VCC that are issued in respect of
-- src:2658 | that sub‑fund or those sub‑funds; and
-- src:2660 | (b) the reference to voting power in the holding company is to
-- src:2661 | the voting power in the umbrella VCC that are exercisable
-- src:2662 | in respect of that sub‑fund or those sub‑funds.
@ref s 44(1A) (src:2651-2662)
GIVEN `the holding company is an umbrella VCC whose holding in the company is attributable to sub-funds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(1A) the shares and voting power referred to are those of the umbrella VCC in respect of those sub-funds` MEANS
    IF `the holding company is an umbrella VCC whose holding in the company is attributable to sub-funds` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2666 | (2) Where the Minister does not grant his or her approval under
-- src:2667 | subsection (1) for a company to hold a relevant licence (whether the
-- src:2668 | licence is granted before, on or after 2 September 2002), the
-- src:2669 | Authority must, within such time and in such manner as the Minister
-- src:2670 | may specify, cancel the licence by written notice and without any
-- src:2671 | compensation.
@ref s 44(2) (src:2666-2671)
GIVEN `the Minister does not grant approval for the company to hold a relevant licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(2) the Authority must, within the time and in the manner the Minister specifies, cancel the licence by written notice and without any compensation` MEANS
    IF `the Minister does not grant approval for the company to hold a relevant licence` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2676 | (3) For the purposes of this section —
-- src:2678 | (a) a person holds a share if —
-- src:2680 | (i) the person is deemed to have an interest in that share
-- src:2681 | under section 7(6) to (10) of the Companies
-- src:2682 | Act 1967; or
-- src:2684 | (ii) the person otherwise has a legal or an equitable
-- src:2685 | interest in that share except for any interest that is to
-- src:2686 | be disregarded under section 7(6) to (10) of the
-- src:2687 | Companies Act 1967;
-- src:2689 | (b) a reference to the control of a percentage of the voting
-- src:2690 | power in a broadcasting company is a reference to the
-- src:2691 | control, whether direct or indirect, of that percentage of the
-- src:2692 | total number of votes that might be cast in a general
-- src:2693 | meeting of the broadcasting company.
@ref s 44(3)(a) and (b) (src:2676-2693)
GIVEN `the person is deemed to have an interest in the share under section 7(6) to (10) of the Companies Act 1967, or otherwise has a legal or an equitable interest in it other than an interest to be disregarded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(3)(a) the person holds the share` MEANS
    `the person is deemed to have an interest in the share under section 7(6) to (10) of the Companies Act 1967, or otherwise has a legal or an equitable interest in it other than an interest to be disregarded`

-- Paragraph (b): a reference to the control of a percentage of the voting power is to control, direct or indirect, of that percentage of the total votes that might be cast in a general meeting.
GIVEN `the control, direct or indirect, is of that percentage of the total number of votes that might be cast in a general meeting of the broadcasting company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(3)(b) the reference to control of a percentage of the voting power is satisfied` MEANS
    `the control, direct or indirect, is of that percentage of the total number of votes that might be cast in a general meeting of the broadcasting company`

-- src:2695 | (4) The application of subsection (3)(a) in relation to any share in a
-- src:2696 | VCC is subject to the following modifications:
-- src:2698 | (a) paragraph (ca) of section 7(9) of the Companies Act 1967
-- src:2699 | does not apply;
-- src:2701 | (b) a book-entry security is treated as an interest in a share;
-- src:2703 | (c) a person that is a subsidiary of a VCC does not have an
-- src:2704 | interest in the shares of the VCC by reason only that that
-- src:2705 | interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the
-- src:2706 | subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act.
@ref s 44(4) (src:2695-2706)
GIVEN `it is a book-entry security in a VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(4) it is treated as an interest in a share` MEANS
    IF `it is a book-entry security in a VCC` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Modification (a): paragraph (ca) of section 7(9) of the Companies Act 1967 does not apply to a share in a VCC.
GIVEN `the share is in a VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(4)(a) paragraph (ca) of section 7(9) of the Companies Act 1967 applies in applying it to the share` MEANS
    IF `the share is in a VCC` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Modification: a subsidiary of a VCC does not have an interest in the shares of the VCC by reason only that the interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act.
GIVEN `the share is in a VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a subsidiary of the VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is the only reason it is said to have an interest in the shares of the VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(4)(c) the subsidiary of a VCC has an interest in the shares of the VCC` MEANS
    IF `the share is in a VCC` AND `the person is a subsidiary of the VCC` AND `the interest is purchased or otherwise acquired by the subsidiary under section 22(6) or (11) of the VCC Act` AND `that is the only reason it is said to have an interest in the shares of the VCC` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `45. Appeal under this Part`

-- src:2712 | 45. Any person aggrieved by any refusal of the Authority to grant
-- src:2713 | its approval or consent under any provision of this Part may appeal to
-- src:2714 | the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 45 (src:2712-2714)
GIVEN `the person is aggrieved by a refusal of the Authority to grant its approval or consent under a provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45 the person may appeal to the Minister, whose decision is final` MEANS
    `the person is aggrieved by a refusal of the Authority to grant its approval or consent under a provision of this Part`

§ `Context chapeau of section 34(2)`

-- src:1936 | (2) In sections 35 to 42, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 34(2) chapeau (src:1936)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(2) the definitions apply in sections 35 to 42` MEANS
    NOT `the context otherwise requires`
